## Current runtime (last verified 2026-08-09)

- Docker Desktop is running with the WSL 2 Linux engine.
- PostgreSQL 16 is healthy for this Compose project at `localhost:5433`.
  Host port `5432` was already occupied by another `tms-postgres` container;
  Compose-internal traffic still uses `db:5432`.
- API is healthy at `http://localhost:3001/api/health`.
- Web is healthy at `http://localhost:5173`.
- The `migrate` container exits with code 0 after applying migrations; this is expected.
- All 24 Prisma migrations through
  `20260803170000_teacher_portal_learning_workflows` apply successfully from an
  empty database.
- `.env.docker` is local-only and explicitly ignored by Git.
- `.env.docker.example` is the safe tracked template.
- A real local tenant named `Frontend Dev Academy` and its `Main Center` branch
  are provisioned for frontend testing. Credentials remain local-only and are
  not recorded in this file or tracked source.
- The development demo tenant `Pinnacle Demo Academy` and its student fixture
  are seeded in the Compose database. The local student credential was reset
  and verified through Better Auth, but is intentionally not recorded here.
- The demo Parent account is active in the Compose database and its login was
  verified through Better Auth and the authenticated Chrome parent smoke test.
  The local password remains intentionally excluded from tracked memory.
- Port `5173` is currently served by the local webpack development server.
  Starting another web dev process will fail with `EADDRINUSE`; use the existing
  server or stop its process before restarting.
- Direct `npm run dev` from `services/api` does not load the repository-root
  `.env`. Prefer the healthy Compose API, which receives its required auth and
  database environment through Compose.
- On 2026-08-09 the Compose API image was rebuilt from the current source and
  reported healthy. An unauthenticated request to
  `/api/finances/billing-ledger` returned `401 Authentication required`, which
  verifies that the route exists and is protected. Before the rebuild, the old
  image returned `404 Cannot GET /api/finances/billing-ledger`.
- `PLATFORM_ADMIN_ENABLED=false` after provisioning. Re-enable it only when a
  new local tenant must be provisioned, then disable it again.

Start/check the stack:

```powershell
docker compose --env-file .env.docker up --build -d
docker compose --env-file .env.docker ps -a
docker compose --env-file .env.docker logs --tail 200
```

Do not use `docker compose down -v` unless intentionally deleting the local
Docker database volume.

## Completed backend work

- Global JSON request limits now cap general API bodies at 256 KiB and legacy
  password-reset bodies at 16 KiB. Malformed JSON returns a safe 400 response,
  oversized payloads return 413, and both include the existing correlation ID.
- Added a dependency-free strict input-schema boundary for legacy password-reset
  requests. It rejects non-object payloads, unknown fields, invalid email/OTP/
  token values, and oversized password values before route business logic runs.
  `npm run test:request-validation --workspace @tms/api` covers this boundary.
- The first high-risk rollout now also validates manual invoice-payment
  references, admission and staff/student account provisioning payloads, and
  teacher GPS IN/OUT attendance payloads. GPS coordinates must be finite and
  in geographic bounds; these endpoints reject unknown fields before any
  authorization or database mutation.
- The next rollout validates NepalPay webhook identifiers/status/amounts,
  petty-cash requests, decisions, approval remarks and receipt URLs, bounded
  student attendance sheets, daily session updates, and the full tenant-policy
  settings contract (including enum values, scalar ranges, and performance
  weight keys). Flexible leave-policy content remains constrained to a JSON
  object so policy evolution does not require client-side hacks.
- Appointment requests/responses, certificate templates/issuance/downloads,
  parent-teacher messages, and student performance scores/remarks were already
  backed by persisted Prisma models and active routes. Broadcast persistence is
  now provided by migration `20260803090000_broadcast_persistence` and scoped
  `POST /api/communication/broadcast` / `GET /api/communication/broadcasts`
  endpoints. `GET /api/performance/staff/scores` now returns the existing
  `StaffPerformanceScore` records, scoped to the caller's tenant and branches.
- Docker Compose stack for PostgreSQL, migration runner, API, and web.
- Prisma/OpenSSL support in the API Docker build and runtime images.
- API workspace dependencies, including Better Auth, copied into the runtime image.
- Duplicate `User.twoFactorEnabled` operation removed from the Better Auth migration.
- Web Docker health probe uses explicit IPv4 loopback and reports healthy.
- Better Auth trusts only the configured `WEB_ORIGIN`; no wildcard origin.
- Authenticated tenant context comes from the verified session, not request headers.
- Branch-scoped middleware is default-deny when no explicit branch is proven.
- Webhook signature, amount, replay, tenant, and invoice protections.
- Cron restricted to tenant-wide Tenant Admin and tenant-scoped mutations.
- Simulation/fail-open route behavior removed; there are no remaining API 501 routes.
- Tenant policy versions and historical policy snapshots added.
- Petty-cash final decisions now support Tenant Admin release, rejection, and
  send-back-for-revision with remarks and atomic status transitions. Migration
  `20260729150000_tenant_admin_petty_cash_decisions` adds `REJECTED`.
- Financial forecast uses current tenant enrollments, course monthly fees,
  current-month paid invoices, and observed dropout rate rather than hard-coded
  demonstration values.
- Manual-only refunds and payroll reconciliation; TMS does not send refund or salary funds.
- connectIPS is inbound-only and validates payments with NCHL before confirmation.
- Admission accounts remain inactive until the admission invoice is paid.
- Only Tenant Admin or the assigned Branch Admin may issue student/parent credentials.
- UKG-Class 10 grade billing, Class 11/12 subject billing, and extra-activity billing rules.
- Invoice PAN/VAT, refund, leave, petty-cash, and other applicable policy snapshots.
- Conditional atomic transitions for invoice payment, refund approval/settlement,
  petty-cash approval/receipt/closure, and payroll approval/reconciliation.
- Remaining workflow transitions hardened with conditional writes and atomic
  transactions: admission credential issuance, onboarding approval/rejection,
  HR clearance/settlement, teacher daily updates, homework submission/grading,
  OTP/reset-token consumption, user deactivation, NepalPay confirmation, and
  connectIPS success/failure reconciliation.
- Database uniqueness now enforces one homework submission per student/assignment
  and globally unique non-null external invoice transaction references.
- Refund request IDOR fixed: student/course tenant ownership and caller authorization
  are verified before creating the request.
- Invoice payment authorization fixed so assigned accountants pass explicit
  resource-level branch authorization.
- Resource-by-ID authorization now resolves ownership from the stored resource
  before access: course/class/enrollment mutations, class/timetable reads,
  student invoice lists, NepalPay QR reads, teacher-session updates, and every
  homework create/submit/grade/read path enforce tenant plus branch or direct
  student/parent/teacher relationships.
- Social-media management was removed by product decision: no API route, server
  mount, Prisma models, permissions, navigation entries, configuration secret,
  encryption helper, or integration cases remain. Migration
  `20260728230000_remove_social_media` removes existing social tables and enum.
- Prisma seeding now uses `prisma/seed-runner.cjs`, which compiles the TypeScript
  seed to temporary CommonJS, executes it, and removes the temporary output.
  The documented Docker `npm run db:seed` command works on Node 20 without the
  previous `.ts` ESM loader failure.

## Completed Tenant Admin web work

- Added `/tenant/control-center` for versioned institution policies, operational
  thresholds, live performance-weight validation, finance signals, calendar,
  and institution-wide HR document alerts.
- Added a typed HTTP foundation in `apps/web/src/services/api/client.ts`:
  - build-time API base URL via `TMS_API_BASE_URL`, defaulting locally to
    `http://localhost:3001/api`;
  - Better Auth cookies on every request;
  - `ApiError` with HTTP status, safe message, and field errors;
  - intentional handling for 401/403/404/409/429/501;
  - safe redirect to login after a 401.
- Added typed domain clients for finance, HR, resources, and academic events.
- Added shared page-level loading, empty, error, retry, denied, and unavailable
  states in `components/patterns/RemoteState.tsx`.
- Added real focused Tenant Admin routes:
  - `/tenant/admissions`: admission creation, inactive-account state, admission
    payment recording, payment-gated credential issuance, and one-time secure
    credential acknowledgement;
  - `/tenant/petty-cash`: filters, Level 2 release, reject/send-back remarks,
    approval history, receipt-state visibility, and closure;
  - `/tenant/payroll`: period calculation, approval for external payment, and
    mandatory-reference manual reconciliation;
  - `/tenant/pl-reports`: P&L, expenses, forecast, rule-based signals, and
    authenticated CSV ledger download;
  - `/tenant/hr-management`: 30-day document-expiry alerts and an explicit
    unavailable state for exit queues lacking list/detail contracts;
  - `/tenant/resource-logs`: branch filtering and policy-snapshot escalation;
  - `/tenant/academic-calendar`: tenant-wide event create/list with an
    institution-wide read-only badge.
- `/tenant/settings` uses the real versioned finance-policy contract; advanced
  policy values are preserved when the dashboard updates basic values.
- Removed misleading Tenant Admin navigation for messages, appointments,
  leave-management queues, arbitrary RBAC editing, and integrations while their
  contracts are unavailable or intentionally return 501.
- Unsupported workflows are documented in
  `documents/frontend-handoffs/TENANT_ADMIN_API_GAPS.md`: refund queues,
  long-sick leave queues, staff-exit queues, certificate template management,
  and calendar update/delete lifecycle.
- Updated `apps/web/tests/smoke.js` to support Tenant Admin accounts with or
  without 2FA and verify the critical new routes after real authentication.

## Completed Student web work

- Added the authenticated, role-restricted `/student/*` portal and student
  dashboard navigation.
- Added focused student routes for home, timetable, homework, results,
  attendance, fees, digital ID, certificates, academic calendar, and
  notifications.
- The home dashboard merges all enrolled course categories into today's
  timetable and shows homework due soon, attendance/latest-score/certificate
  summaries, blocked-fee status, and upcoming academic or fee events.
- Homework is read-only and includes functional Pending, Due soon, Overdue,
  and Completed filters with accessible pressed states and honest empty states.
- Results show published scores, class-average comparisons, strongest/weakest
  subject insights, and accessible SVG score-history trend lines.
- Attendance shows Present, Absent, and Absent (Excused) session states and
  explains how approved leave is represented.
- Digital ID shows enrollment, grade, roll number, academic year, validity,
  branch identification guidance, and explicit Active/Blocked status.
- Fees show the current outstanding balance, explicit blocked state,
  color-plus-text payment-cycle states, itemized dues/discounts/fines/net
  payable, and a Nepal Pay QR dialog.
- The Nepal Pay dialog supports close button, backdrop click, Escape, focus
  trapping, body-scroll locking, and focus return to its trigger.
- Certificates remain visible in a permanent history and provide download
  interaction feedback. Calendar views distinguish holidays, exams,
  ceremonies, and fee due dates.
- Notifications cover fee due/overdue, homework, approved parent-applied leave,
  and certificate issuance. Student appointment notifications are deliberately
  excluded because appointments are a parent-teacher flow.
- Student UI supports responsive layouts, keyboard focus visibility, minimum
  touch targets, dark mode, and reduced-motion preferences.
- Canonical web StyleSeed tokens now use the locked `#1560BD` blue,
  `#2F6FED` bright blue, `#002D72` navy, `#FFBC3B` gold, `#F5F7FA` surface,
  `#1B1F3B` text, Fraunces display typography, and Roboto UI typography.
- Primary implementation files:
  `apps/web/src/pages/StudentPortal.tsx`,
  `apps/web/src/features/student/studentPortal.css`,
  `apps/web/src/features/student/studentPortalData.ts`,
  `apps/web/src/router/index.tsx`, and
  `apps/web/src/components/patterns/dashboardNavigation.ts`.
- Student screens currently use frontend fixture data. Real-time teacher score
  updates, live attendance/invoice data, genuine Nepal Pay QR payloads,
  certificate PDF downloads, and push delivery still require student API and
  event integration.

## Completed Parent web work

- Replaced the previous mixed student/parent prototype with a dedicated,
  authenticated, role-restricted `/parent/*` portal.
- Added parent routes for home, timetable, attendance, performance, messages,
  appointments, leave, fees, certificates, academic calendar, and notifications.
- Added a persistent linked-child switcher. The selected child is stored in the
  `child` query parameter, survives refresh/navigation, and scopes every portal
  view independently so sibling records are never merged.
- Added a selected-child context bar showing name, grade, branch, roll number,
  and Active/Blocked status on every parent page.
- The dashboard shows child-specific timetable, attendance, outstanding balance,
  appointments, leave history, approved parent-visible remarks, and events.
- Performance views explicitly filter out internal-only remarks and explain the
  institution visibility boundary.
- Messaging only lists teachers assigned to the selected child's fixture
  classes; threads are keyed by both child and teacher, so the same teacher has
  separate sibling conversations.
- Appointment UI covers individual/group requests, lifecycle states, linked
  alternative times, and client-side rejection inside the default 24-hour
  booking window.
- Leave UI covers planned requests, Approved/Pending states, automatic
  Absent (Excused) explanation, and urgent branch-recorded emergency departures.
- Fees provide a child-specific payment calendar, itemized invoices, explicit
  Blocked status, and a Nepal Pay dialog with backdrop/Escape closing, focus
  trapping, body-scroll locking, and focus restoration.
- Certificates and calendars are scoped per child. Notifications show Push/SMS
  channel badges and reserve urgent visual treatment for fee and emergency events.
- Unsupported writes are not simulated as successes:
  persistent messaging, appointment negotiation, performance persistence,
  authenticated certificate downloads, and safe child-scoped parent leave
  submission are labeled unavailable because their current API contracts are
  missing, return 501, or are not safely child-scoped.
- Added responsive/dark-mode/reduced-motion styling using the locked StyleSeed
  tokens and accessible semantic controls, focus indicators, dialog behavior,
  form labels, validation messages, tables, and empty/unavailable states.
- Added `apps/web/tests/parent-smoke.js`, which authenticates a demo Parent and
  verifies child switching, non-merged timetable data, assigned-teacher privacy,
  24-hour appointment validation, and Nepal Pay dialog Escape behavior.
- The newly implemented Parent portal is available after login at
  `/parent/home`; all parent workspace routes preserve the selected child using
  the `child` query parameter.
- Primary implementation files:
  `apps/web/src/pages/ParentStudentPortal.tsx`,
  `apps/web/src/features/parent/parentPortal.css`,
  `apps/web/src/features/parent/parentPortalData.ts`,
  `apps/web/src/features/parent/parentPortalTypes.ts`,
  `apps/web/src/router/index.tsx`, and
  `apps/web/src/components/patterns/dashboardNavigation.ts`.

## Teacher portal implementation

- Rebuilt the authenticated, role-restricted Teacher workspace across
  `/teacher/dashboard`, `/teacher/timetable`, `/teacher/geo-attendance`,
  `/teacher/attendance`, `/teacher/syllabus`, `/teacher/daily-update-log`,
  `/teacher/homework`, `/teacher/results`, `/teacher/profile`,
  `/teacher/leave-requests`, and `/teacher/salary-slips`. The wildcard route now
  renders `TeacherPortal`; it no longer falls through to the generic dashboard
  placeholder.
- Renamed the first navigation item to Teacher Dashboard. Today's classes are
  shown in My Timetable above the complete weekly teaching schedule rather than
  being presented as the dashboard itself.
- Geo Attendance is deliberately a separate future module. The current page
  clearly states that location is not collected there; live Mark IN/OUT controls
  were removed from the dashboard pending the future rollout.
- Added the teacher-scoped `GET /api/teacher/workspace` aggregate for identity,
  attendance statistics/stamps, assigned classes and rosters, sessions,
  syllabi, homework, results, leave history, performance, and payroll history.
- Added live class-attendance submission for assigned classes. Server validation
  rejects foreign roster entries and fee-blocked Present states, normalizes
  overlapping approved student leave to Excused, and atomically replaces that
  teacher's session attendance sheet.
- Added persisted `Syllabus`, `SyllabusChapter`, and `DailyLessonLog` models with
  `IN_PROGRESS`, `COMPLETED`, and `LEFT` status. Teachers create a subject plan
  and update daily chapter progress; enrolled students receive the read-only
  syllabus and progress notes in their Student portal.
- Homework creation now uses the existing assigned-class backend and supports
  text instructions plus an optional small data-URL attachment in the current
  secure preview implementation.
- Results now support class-wide draft creation with full marks, pass marks,
  obtained marks, automatic class percentile, optional result sheet, and an
  explicit `publishedAt` boundary. Student results remain hidden until shared.
  Result History groups rows by assessment/date and provides one Share All
  action for every remaining draft in the selected grade/class, while retaining
  Share One for exceptions.
- Added Teacher profile/employment detail, own performance summary, unmerged
  attendance-stamp history, leave submission/history, upcoming salary, and
  salary-slip history. Payroll remains read-only and teacher-scoped.
- Added realistic sample data for empty or partially seeded Teacher accounts.
  Live API records take precedence, and a visible Sample Data Preview banner
  identifies any demonstration content.
- Added accessible labels, semantic controls, visible focus treatment, loading,
  error, empty/locked states, 40px-or-larger touch targets, mobile safe-area
  spacing, responsive layouts, and reduced-motion handling.
- Added migration `20260803170000_teacher_portal_learning_workflows` and the
  build/QA document `documents/TEACHER_PORTAL_WEB_FUNCTIONAL_SPEC.md`.
- Added `apps/web/tests/teacher-smoke.js` for authenticated teacher verification
  of the fee-blocked/approved-leave roster states and unmerged AUTO-OUT/RE-IN
  history. Its authenticated assertions require `TMS_TEACHER_EMAIL` and
  `TMS_TEACHER_PASSWORD`.
- Demo teacher login email is `teacher@demo.tms.local`, but the current
  `SEED_DEMO=true` seed hashes a random UUID and intentionally never prints it.
  Manual login therefore requires creating/resetting a Teacher password or
  adding a local-only configurable demo password before reseeding.
- Primary implementation files:
  `apps/web/src/pages/TeacherPortal.tsx`,
  `apps/web/src/features/teacher/teacherPortal.css`,
  `apps/web/src/features/teacher/teacherPortalData.ts`,
  `apps/web/src/features/teacher/teacherPortalTypes.ts`, and
  `apps/web/tests/teacher-smoke.js`.

