## Shared billing and payroll ledger (2026-08-09)

- Added authenticated `GET /api/finances/billing-ledger`. Tenant Admin receives
  tenant-wide data; Accountants are scoped by signed `manage_billing` branch
  assignments; an assigned `Branch Admin` role itself grants billing access only
  to that role's branch, even when its permission array omits `manage_billing`.
- Added persisted `POST /api/finances/billing-ledger/invoices` and
  `POST /api/finances/billing-ledger/payrolls`. They use the same tenant/branch
  billing scope as ledger reads; invoice payment recording and student invoice
  access also recognize assigned Branch Admin scope. Writes go through Prisma
  and therefore appear across all authorized role portals after refresh.
  Duplicate teacher/month payrolls are rejected with `409`.
- The ledger returns complete posted invoice details: invoice type, base amount,
  discount, fine, net payable, VAT snapshot, cycle dates, due date, payment
  date/reference, overdue derivation, status, and creation time.
- Student projections derive monthly tuition from the assigned grade plus
  eligible active course/activity fees and show future cycles only within the
  one-year course window derived from admission date. Projections are labelled
  as forecasts and are not persisted as debts or payable invoices.
- Teacher history uses persisted Payroll records. The next-month projection is
  derived from the active staff salary structure; bonuses and deductions remain
  zero until payroll is posted. Fixed salaries use `basicSalary`; hourly
  contracts use `hourlyRate * expectedMonthlyHours` when configured.
- Added typed client contracts in `apps/web/src/services/api.ts` and the shared
  UI at `apps/web/src/components/finance/SharedBillingWorkspace.tsx`.
  `BranchAdminWorkspace.tsx` and `StaffFinancePage.tsx` both render this shared
  component, preventing role-specific billing behavior from drifting.
- Tenant Admin P&L/reporting now reads the same persisted billing ledger and
  displays all branch invoice/payroll records plus derived institution tuition,
  payroll, collection, and margin projections. The obsolete in-memory global
  ledger calls are no longer used by active portal code.
- Tenant Admin `/tenant/fees` keeps the student `View` action enabled even when
  `invoiceCount` is zero. Opening the drawer loads the shared ledger profile in
  parallel with posted invoices, shows the student's billing plan and future
  projections, and renders an explicit no-invoice-history state when applicable.
- Research basis: subscription schedules/upcoming amounts remain projections
  until an invoice is created; posted invoices remain historical financial
  records. This follows the lifecycle distinction documented by Stripe Billing.

